<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌧️ LIVE PRECIPITATION</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE PRECIPITATION</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/precipitation/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>Precipitation intensity (NEXRAD N0Q base reflectivity, dBZ, OBSERVED radar echo): <b>LOWEST 5 Very Light</b> cyan/blue (drizzle, mist) &rarr; <b>Light</b> greens (~20-30: light rain/snow) &rarr; <b>Moderate</b> dark green (~30-40: steady rain/snow) &rarr; <b>Heavy</b> yellow/orange (~40-50: heavy rain) &rarr; <b>Severe</b> red (~50-60: severe storms, hail possible) &rarr; <b>Intense</b> magenta/purple (~60-70: violent storms, large hail) &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 70+ Extreme</b> white (destructive hail, debris). Same dBZ always shows the same color in every season — rain, snow, lake-effect snow, thunderstorms. No echo (no precipitation) stays see-through so the map underneath shows.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: Iowa Environmental Mesonet (Iowa State University) CONUS NEXRAD N0Q Base Reflectivity mosaic from NOAA NWS WSR-88D Level-III (5-minute updates)).<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-27 18:05 UTC<br/><b>Source version:</b> iem-n0q-20260927-1805<br/><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT OBSERVATION (NEXRAD 5-min mosaic)</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>🌧️ LIVE PRECIPITATION — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/Great_Lakes_Live_Precipitation.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>30</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
